Subject: [PATCH] netifyd: drop stale nfnetlink probe from load_modules()

Since Linux 7.3 NETFILTER_NETLINK is a bool symbol, compiled into
the core image with no module scaffolding (no .ko, no sysfs entry,
no alias): the modprobe in load_modules() fails on every boot
("failed to find a module named nfnetlink") and can never succeed.
On pre-7.3 kernels the probe is redundant with kmodloader autoload
when kmod-nfnetlink is installed, and rescues nothing when it is
not (the subsystem is then missing and conntrack is broken with or
without the probe). Delete the line; the nf_conntrack_netlink
probe below it is unaffected (real .ko, loads fine). Targets
functions.sh.in (functions.sh is generated by configure); patches
apply before autogen, so the generated file is not present yet.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 deploy/functions.sh.in | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

--- a/deploy/functions.sh.in
+++ b/deploy/functions.sh.in
@@ -187,7 +187,6 @@

 load_modules()
 {
-    modprobe nfnetlink >/dev/null 2>&1
     modprobe nf_conntrack_netlink >/dev/null 2>&1
 }

